   "level": "info",
   "product": "*",
   "title": {
    "en": "November Moon: New on the 9th, Full on the 24th"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "New Moon on Nov 9 at about 16:00 JST (07:00 UT) and Full Moon on Nov 24 at about 23:50 JST (14:50 UT). Computed values, a few minutes of error. The days around New Moon give the darkest skies. (Test notice)"
   }
  },
  {
   "date": "2026-10-28",
   "level": "info",
   "product": "*",
   "title": {
    "en": "Leonids: best around Nov 17-18"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "The Leonids usually peak around Nov 17-18, about 15 meteors per hour under good conditions. This year the Moon is near first quarter on the 17th and sets after midnight, so the pre-dawn sky is dark. The radiant in Leo rises after midnight. (Test notice)"
   }
  },
  {
   "date": "2026-10-28",
   "level": "info",
   "product": "*",
   "title": {
    "en": "Taurids: about Nov 5 (south) and Nov 12 (north)"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "Only a few meteors per hour, but slow, bright fireballs are a feature. On Nov 5 only a thin crescent rises before dawn, and on Nov 12 the thin Moon sets early in the evening, so both nights are dark. (Test notice)"
   }
  }
 ]
